[{"id":69634,"sender_id":16,"sender_full_name":"SimonWillerton","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/94692fa5304a0c2e03686f7d37651544?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/5-nLab-General-Discussions/topic/Enriched.20bicategory.20of.20V-profunctors/near/69634\">#1</a> Is the enriched bicategory of <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>V</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">V</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\">V</span></span></span></span>-profunctors considered in the literature anywhere?  Here I want <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>V</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">V</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\">V</span></span></span></span> to be, say, a complete, cocomplete, closed, symmetric monoidal category; and by enriched bicategory I mean <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>V</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">V</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\">V</span></span></span></span>-enriched at the 2-cell level, or, equivalenty, <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>V</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">V</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\">V</span></span></span></span>-cat enriched at the hom level.</p>\n<p>At the <a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/enriched+bicategory\">enriched bicategory</a> page, three of the interesting looking references are seemingly unavailable, namely Sean Carmody’s thesis, Steve Lack’s thesis and Alex Hoffnung’s notes.  Does anyone know if these are online anywhere?  (I realise I could email Steve or Alex, but having links from the nlab page would be even better.)</p>\n<p>This ought to be a protoytpical example of a <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>V</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">V</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\">V</span></span></span></span>-cat enriched bicategory, and it would be nice if someone has already proved it!</p>","timestamp":1533556408,"subject":"Enriched bicategory of V-profunctors","stream_id":5,"display_recipient":"nLab General Discussions","reactions":[]},{"id":69636,"sender_id":10,"sender_full_name":"Mike Shulman","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/ede34282f405f902e12fa7e6cf336572?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/5-nLab-General-Discussions/topic/Enriched.20bicategory.20of.20V-profunctors/near/69636\">#2</a> Good question, but I don’t know the answer offhand.</p>","timestamp":1533583170,"subject":"Enriched bicategory of V-profunctors","stream_id":5,"display_recipient":"nLab General Discussions","reactions":[]}]